<title>UK: Tokyo keeps top place for airport charges.</title>
<headline>Tokyo keeps top place for airport charges.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo-Narita has the world's most expensive airport charges, followed by New Jersey-Newark and Chicago, a study by London-based transport consultants Symonds, Travers Morgan shows.</p>
<p>The 40 airports covered in the eighth annual edition of the study show Tokyo tops the &quot;charges index&quot; at 100, followed by New Jersey at 80, Chicago 74, Vienna 69 and New York-JFK at 66.</p>
<p>Last year's survey also had Tokyo at 100 with New Jersey at 67, Chicago at 65, Frankfurt at 62 and Vienna at 60.</p>
<p>Other changes saw Moscow rise to the 8th most expensive airport (from 13), Miami to 18th from 22nd and Dallas at 31st against 35th.</p>
<p>Heathrow and Gatwick were ranked as 27th and 34th respectively and the lowest ranked -- in descending order - were Hong Kong, Sydney San Francisco, Jeddah, and Dubai, with the latter's costs only seven percent of Tokyo's.</p>
<p>The index is calculated by taking charges for turning round a sample of eight different aircraft types at each of the 40 airports at the start of June.</p>
<p>The changes in the index reflects the impact of both currency movements and changes to actual charges.</p>
